Net cash used in operating activities was $0.7 million for the nine months ended April 30, 2026, compared to net cash provided by operating activities of $1.4 million for the nine months ended April 30, 2025, representing an increase in cash used in operating activities of approximately $2.1 million. The increase in net cash used in operating activities was primarily attributable to the following:

• Non-cash adjustments to reconcile net income to net cash provided by operating activities were $401,025 in the nine months ended April 30, 2026, compared to $534,842 in the nine months ended April 30, 2025. These adjustments primarily consisted of depreciation, non-cash operating lease expense, deferred taxes, loss on disposal of equipment, and accrued interest expense on related-party loans;

• An increase in accounts receivable of $1.0 million in the nine months ended April 30, 2026, compared to a decrease of $222 in the nine months ended April 30, 2025;

• A decrease in operating leases liabilities of $152,917 in the nine months ended April 30, 2026, compared to a decrease of $197,875 in the nine months ended April 30, 2025;

• A decrease in accounts payable of $116,935 in the nine months ended April 30, 2026, compared to a decrease of $42,187 in the nine months ended April 30, 2025;

